  "reason": "The strongest evidence points to scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l as the optimal encoder pair, with transformer aggregation + weighted fusion yielding the best result (0.725, config_045). Both fusion variants (weighted and concat) with transformer aggregation have been tested. The remaining untested variant with this encoder pair is the singleprofile setting (config_002), which removes the aggregation step entirely and fuses a single RNA representation directly with the image representation. This is the most architecturally distinct untested option within the best encoder combination. While multiprofile has been consistently superior in our experiments, the singleprofile variant is genuinely unexplored with the top encoders and represents the largest remaining source of uncertainty. Weighted fusion is chosen over concat based on the slight edge observed in multiprofile (0.725 vs 0.721). As the final experiment, this maximizes the chance of discovering an unexpected improvement or confirms that the current best (0.725) is robust."
}

